ץ","tr":"sha·rats","gloss":"to swarm","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H0854","lemma":"אֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":929},{"base":"H6105","lemma":"עָצֹם","tr":"a·tsom","gloss":"be vast","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H6509","lemma":"פָּרָה","tr":"pa·rah","gloss":"be fruitful","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":29},{"base":"H3409","lemma":"יָרֵךְ","tr":"ya·rekh","gloss":"thigh","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"“I am God,” He said, “the God of your father. Do not be afraid to go down to Egypt, for I will make you into a great nation there.","from":7},{"book":"DEU","chapter":10,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Your fathers went down to Egypt, seventy in all, and now the LORD your God has made you as numerous as the stars in the sky.","from":5},{"book":"GEN","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"God blessed them and said to them, “Be fruitful and multiply, and fill the earth and subdue it; rule over the fish of the sea and the birds of the air and every creature that crawls upon the earth.”","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Now these are the names of the sons of Israel (Jacob and his descendants) who went to Egypt: Reuben, Jacobʼs firstborn.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"All those belonging to Jacob who came to Egypt—his direct descendants, besides the wives of Jacobʼs sons—numbered sixty-six persons.","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":26,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"and you are to declare before the LORD your God, “My father was a wandering Aramean, and he went down to Egypt few in number and lived there and became a great nation, mighty and numerous.","from":7},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"These were the sons of Israel: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Zebulun,","from":1},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, and Asher.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":12}]},"8-14":{"people":[{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547i","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"pithom-h6619","name":"Pithom","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"raamses-h7486h","name":"Raamses","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"H6531","lemma":"פֶּ֫רֶךְ","tr":"pe·rekh","gloss":"severity","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H5656","lemma":"עֲבֹדָה","tr":"a·vo·dah","gloss":"service","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":145},{"base":"H6031","lemma":"עָנָה","tr":"a·nah","gloss":"be occupied","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":82},{"base":"H7235","lemma":"רָבָה","tr":"ra·vah","gloss":"to multiply","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":227},{"base":"H5647","lemma":"עָבַד","tr":"a·vad","gloss":"to serve","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":288},{"base":"H7486","lemma":"רַֽעַמְסֵס","tr":"ra·me·ses","gloss":"Rameses","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H5450","lemma":"סִבְלָה","tr":"se·va·lah","gloss":"burden","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H4543","lemma":"מִסְכְּנוֹת","tr":"mis·ke·nah","gloss":"storage","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H6973","lemma":"קוּץ","tr":"quts","gloss":"to loathe","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H3651","lemma":"כֵּן","tr":"ken","gloss":"right","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":765}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordsaid to Abram, “Know for certain that your descendants will be strangers in a land that is not their own, and they will be enslaved and mistreated four hundred years.","from":11},{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And the LORD made His people very fruitful, more numerous than their foes,","from":12},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Then another king, who knew nothing of Joseph, arose over Egypt.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":47,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So Joseph settled his father and brothers in the land of Egypt and gave them property in the best part of the land, the district of Rameses, as Pharaoh had commanded.","from":11},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"One day, after Moses had grown up, he went out to his own people and observed their hard labor. He saw an Egyptian beating a Hebrew, one of his own people.","from":11},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The LORD said, “I have indeed seen the affliction of My people in Egypt. I have heard them crying out because of their oppressors, and I am aware of their sufferings.","from":11},{"book":"NUM","chapter":20,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"how our fathers went down to Egypt, where we lived many years. The Egyptians mistreated us and our fathers,","from":14},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He exploited our people and oppressed our fathers, forcing them to abandon their infants so they would die.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"15-22":{"people":[{"id":"hebrews-h5680","name":"Hebrews","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"puah-h6326","name":"Puah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"shiphrah-h8236","name":"Shiphrah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547i","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":2,"firstVerse":19}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"nile-h2975g","name":"Nile","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22}],"words":[{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":496},{"base":"H5680","lemma":"עִבְרִי","tr":"iv·ri","gloss":"Hebrew","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":34},{"base":"H2421","lemma":"חָיָה","tr":"cha·yah","gloss":"to live","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":282},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":641},{"base":"H3206","lemma":"יֶ֫לֶד","tr":"ye·led","gloss":"youth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":89},{"base":"H6547","lemma":"פַּרְעֹה","tr":"par·oh","gloss":"Pharaoh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":274},{"base":"H3372","lemma":"יָרֵא","tr":"ya·re","gloss":"to fear","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":315},{"base":"H0070","lemma":"אֹבֶן","tr":"o·ven","gloss":"wheel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3209","lemma":"יִלּוֹד","tr":"yil·lod","gloss":"born","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","tr":"bat","gloss":"daughter","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":588}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men.","from":17},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"If you listen to all that I command you, walk in My ways, and do what is right in My sight in order to keep My statutes and commandments as My servant David did, then I will be with you. I will build you a lasting dynasty just as I built for David, and I will give Israel to you.","from":21},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Do not be afraid of those who kill the body but cannot kill the soul. Instead, fear the One who can destroy both soul and body in hell.","from":17},{"book":"LUK","chapter":12,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"But I will show you whom you should fear: Fear the One who, after you have been killed, has authority to throw you into hell. Yes, I tell you, fear Him!","from":17},{"book":"ECC","chapter":12,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"When all has been heard, the conclusion of the matter is this: Fear God and keep His commandments, because this is the whole duty of man.","from":17},{"book":"1SA","chapter":2,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Then I will raise up for Myself a faithful priest. He will do whatever is in My heart and mind. And I will build for him an enduring house, and he will walk before My anointed one for all time.","from":21},{"book":"PSA","chapter":37,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Trust in the LORD and do good; dwell in the land and cultivate faithfulness.","from":21},{"book":"ECC","chapter":8,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Although a sinner does evil a hundred times and still lives long, yet I also know that it will go well with those who fear God, who are reverent in His presence.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}